  "headline": "A trained noise-aware PFN on label-RR releases recovers 71-86% of the exact noise-aware NLL gain over naive plug-in at n=128 (NLL 0.623/0.575/0.554 vs naive 0.644/0.604/0.565), with unchanged accuracy and no cost on clean data (max NLL difference 0.0002). The naive PFN matches the exact naive target (KL <= 0.0013), i.e. it is under-confident as Prop. D2 predicts.",
